<node id="11141900" title="How to redefine a modules private function?" created="2022-03-07 22:01:25" updated="2022-03-07 22:01:25" _doctext_mode="lenient"><type id="115">perlquestion</type>
<author id="1145534">sectokia</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;p&gt;In AnyEvent::DNS code there is this line that sets the port for the DNS server (and there seems to be no way to specify another port):&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;code&gt;
sub DOMAIN_PORT() { 53 } # if this changes drop me a note
&lt;/code&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I want to use another port. I thought I could simply re-define it like so:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;code&gt;
*AnyEvent::DNS::DOMAIN_PORT = sub () { 8053 };
print AnyEvent::DNS::DOMAIN_PORT(); # Prints 53..
&lt;/code&gt;

&lt;p&gt;However it doesn't work. What am I doing wrong?&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
